---
source: crates/daemon/tests/integration/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Talk to the assistant about your mail. It reads and searches freely; every change it wants to make waits for your approval

Usage: mxr assistant [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status   Whether the assistant can run, and on which model
  model    The model the assistant uses: list the choices, or set one for every conversation. Hosted models need their key (`mxr llm key set`)
  send     Send a message, starting a conversation unless --conversation is given, and wait for the reply. Changes the assistant wants to make, and questions it asks, are printed with the command that answers them
  approve  Approve a change the assistant is waiting on. It runs exactly the call shown
  reject   Decline a change or question; nothing runs
  answer   Answer a question the assistant asked. For one question, use --choose and/or --other; for several, --answers-json
  trust    Let reversible changes (archive, move, star, read, labels) run without asking in one conversation. Sending, deleting, trash, spam and rules always ask
  stop     Stop a running turn, or close what is waiting without running it
  list     Conversations, most recently active first
  show     Show a whole conversation
  delete   Delete a conversation and its transcript
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>  [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help             Print help
